IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`
IMPORT `cbr-reg1`
IMPORT `cbr-reg2-benefits`
IMPORT `cbr-reg2-couples`
IMPORT `cbr-reg2-rate`

-- TESTS OF REGULATION 2(1) AND (4), AND OF THE ORDER IN WHICH PARAGRAPHS (1)(a), (4),
-- (5) AND (2) ARE APPLIED (src:18-38). Every expected value is written from the text,
-- with its reason, before the run. The cases marked FORK are the ones where the text
-- is silent on which paragraph prevails: they assert the reading taken (NOTES.md,
-- forks F1 and F2), so that a reviewer who reads the text the other way sees at once
-- which assertions change.
--
-- The figures: £27.05 is "the enhanced rate" (reg 2(1)(a)), £17.90 is "any other
-- case" (reg 2(1)(b)).

§ `Tests of regulation 2(1) and (4)`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN voluntary IS A BOOLEAN
      spouse IS A BOOLEAN
      partner IS A BOOLEAN
      polya IS A BOOLEAN
      polyb IS A BOOLEAN
      residing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Claimant at the start of the week`
`a claimant with the facts` voluntary spouse partner polya polyb residing MEANS
    `Claimant at the start of the week` WITH
        `a voluntary organisation` IS voluntary
        `living with the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS spouse
        `living with another person as the claimant's spouse or civil partner` IS partner
        `during the marriage a party to it is married to more than one person` IS polya
        `the ceremony of the marriage took place under the law of a country which permits polygamy` IS polyb
        `residing with other members of that marriage` IS residing

`a claimant living alone` MEANS `a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a voluntary organisation` MEANS `a claimant with the facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a claimant living with a spouse` MEANS `a claimant with the facts` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A child or qualifying young person, built from the facts the rules read: date of
-- birth; a child for child benefit; where; qualifying young person under SSCBA; under
-- SSCB(NI)A; the only, elder or eldest child paid for; the claimant resides with a
-- parent of the child; and does so as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a).
GIVEN born IS A DATE
      ischild IS A BOOLEAN
      place IS A `Where a young person is`
      sscba IS A BOOLEAN
      sscbni IS A BOOLEAN
      eldest IS A BOOLEAN
      withparent IS A BOOLEAN
      ascouple IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
`a person with the facts` born ischild place sscba sscbni eldest withparent ascouple MEANS
    `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week` WITH
        `date of birth` IS born
        `child benefit is payable to the claimant in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS TRUE
        `a child for the purposes of child benefit` IS ischild
        `where the young person is` IS place
        `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCBA` IS sscba
        `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A` IS sscbni
        `the only person, or the elder or eldest person, in respect of whom child benefit is payable to the claimant` IS eldest
        `the claimant resides with a parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS withparent
        `the claimant resides with that parent as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)` IS ascouple

-- The same facts, but child benefit is not payable for the child (entitlement is the
-- parent Act's, out of text).
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
`a child for whom child benefit is not payable, born on` born MEANS
    `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week` WITH
        `date of birth` IS born
        `child benefit is payable to the claimant in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS FALSE
        `a child for the purposes of child benefit` IS TRUE
        `where the young person is` IS `in Great Britain`
        `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCBA` IS FALSE
        `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A` IS FALSE
        `the only person, or the elder or eldest person, in respect of whom child benefit is payable to the claimant` IS TRUE
        `the claimant resides with a parent of the child or qualifying young person` IS FALSE
        `the claimant resides with that parent as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)` IS FALSE

-- A child, in Great Britain, born on the date: the only or eldest (or not).
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
`the only or eldest child born on` born MEANS `a person with the facts` born TRUE `in Great Britain` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
`a younger child born on` born MEANS `a person with the facts` born TRUE `in Great Britain` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
`the only or eldest child, living with a parent of the child, born on` born MEANS `a person with the facts` born TRUE `in Great Britain` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
`the only or eldest child, living with the child's parent as a couple, born on` born MEANS `a person with the facts` born TRUE `in Great Britain` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE

-- A payment: its kind; whether receipt entitles to a Schedule 4 increase; the
-- instrument; whether the Commissioners accept it as analogous; paid to the claimant;
-- paid for the child.
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of payment made for the week`
      entitles IS A BOOLEAN
      accepted IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A BOOLEAN
      forchild IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment made for the week`
`a payment of kind` kind entitles accepted paid forchild MEANS
    `Payment made for the week` WITH
        `kind of payment` IS kind
        `receipt of the benefit entitles the recipient to an increase for dependants specified in the Table in Schedule 4 to that Act` IS entitles
        `instrument granting the allowance` IS `an instrument not listed in paragraph (6)(c)(i) to (vii)`
        `the Commissioners accept the allowance as analogous to one granted under those instruments` IS accepted
        `paid to the claimant in respect of the week` IS paid
        `paid in respect of the child or qualifying young person` IS forchild

`no payment` MEANS `a payment of kind` `a payment of some other kind` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a pension increase for the child` MEANS `a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
`a pension that carries no increase for dependants` MEANS `a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE

GIVEN exists IS A BOOLEAN
      born IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week`
`another person whose child counts` exists born MEANS
    `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week` WITH
        `child benefit would, but for paragraph (2), be payable at the enhanced rate to one of them for another child or qualifying person` IS exists
        `date of birth of the elder or eldest of those other children` IS born

`nobody else` MEANS `another person whose child counts` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)

-- A week in 2026 on or after the version date of the text, and one before.
`a week of 2026` MEANS Date 1 6 2026

-- The rate for the case, in pounds a week, for the given facts.
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      claimant IS A `Claimant at the start of the week`
      child IS A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
      payment IS A `Payment made for the week`
      others IS A `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the weekly rate for` week claimant child payment others MEANS
    `the weekly rate of child benefit under regulation 2 for the child in the week beginning` week claimant child payment others

§§ `Regulation 2(1) (src:18-20): the enhanced rate for the only, elder or eldest child, and £17.90 in any other case`

-- The only child of a person living alone, no payment: the enhanced rate, £27.05.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 27.05
-- Not the only, elder or eldest child: any other case, £17.90.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`a younger child born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 17.90
-- Three children, the case of each: eldest £27.05, the other two £17.90 each.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2005)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 27.05
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`a younger child born on` (Date 1 1 2008)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 17.90
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`a younger child born on` (Date 1 1 2011)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 17.90
-- The case, as the text names it.
#ASSERT `the case under regulation 2(1) for the child in the week beginning` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST `the case for the enhanced rate`
#ASSERT `the case under regulation 2(1) for the child in the week beginning` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`a younger child born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST `any other case`
-- The two figures, as the text states them.
#ASSERT `the enhanced rate` EQUALS 27.05
#ASSERT `the rate in any other case` EQUALS 17.90
#ASSERT `the weekly rate in pounds for the case` `the case for the enhanced rate` EQUALS 27.05
#ASSERT `the weekly rate in pounds for the case` `any other case` EQUALS 17.90

§§ `Regulation 2(4)(a) (src:32-33): not at the enhanced rate if the person is a voluntary organisation`

#ASSERT `paragraph (4)(a) applies to the claimant` `a voluntary organisation`
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (4)(a) applies to the claimant` `a claimant living alone`)
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a voluntary organisation` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 17.90

§§ `Regulation 2(4)(b) (src:34): not at the enhanced rate if the person resides, otherwise than as in paragraph (2)(a), with a parent of the child`

#ASSERT `paragraph (4)(b) applies to the claimant` (`the only or eldest child, living with a parent of the child, born on` (Date 1 1 2010))
-- Not living with a parent of the child: (4)(b) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (4)(b) applies to the claimant` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)))
-- Living with the parent AS mentioned in paragraph (2)(a): the carve-out in the brackets.
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (4)(b) applies to the claimant` (`the only or eldest child, living with the child's parent as a couple, born on` (Date 1 1 2010)))
#ASSERT `paragraph (4) bars the enhanced rate` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child, living with a parent of the child, born on` (Date 1 1 2010))
#ASSERT `paragraph (4) bars the enhanced rate` `a voluntary organisation` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010))
#ASSERT NOT (`paragraph (4) bars the enhanced rate` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)))
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child, living with a parent of the child, born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 17.90
-- The carve-out: with the parent as a couple, nothing is barred. Here the person lives alone as to the couple facts (a claimant who lives with the parent as spouse would also have the spouse fact set; see the couples cases below).
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child, living with the child's parent as a couple, born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 27.05

§§ `Regulation 2(5) (src:35-38) against paragraph (4): FORK F1, the enhanced rate is given back`

-- FORK F1. The person lives with the child's parent (so (4)(b) takes the enhanced rate away) and a specified benefit is paid to them for the only or eldest child: paragraph (5) says the enhanced rate "shall be payable". Reading taken: (5) prevails.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child, living with a parent of the child, born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `a pension increase for the child` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 27.05
-- FORK F1, voluntary organisation: same reading.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a voluntary organisation` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `a pension increase for the child` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 27.05
-- A payment that is not a specified benefit gives nothing back.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child, living with a parent of the child, born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `a pension that carries no increase for dependants` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 17.90
-- A specified benefit paid for a child who is not the only, elder or eldest does not give the enhanced rate for that child ((5)(b)).
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`a younger child born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `a pension increase for the child` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 17.90
-- A specified benefit paid to someone else, or not for this child: not (a), not (b).
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child, living with a parent of the child, born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 17.90
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child, living with a parent of the child, born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) (`a payment of kind` `a benefit under SSCBA` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 17.90
-- Where (4) does not apply, a specified benefit changes nothing: the enhanced rate was payable anyway.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `a pension increase for the child` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 27.05

§§ `Regulation 2(2) (src:21-28): a couple or polygamous household, the enhanced rate for only the elder or eldest`

-- Both would get the enhanced rate: the claimant's child, born 1 January 2010, is the elder of the two children (the other is born 1 January 2012).
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living with a spouse` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2012)) EQUALS JUST 27.05
-- The claimant's child is the younger: any other case, £17.90.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living with a spouse` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST 17.90
-- Born on the same day: the text does not say which is the elder (fork F3): not covered.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living with a spouse` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Born one day apart, each way.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living with a spouse` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 2 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST 27.05
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living with a spouse` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 2 1 2010)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST 17.90
-- (c) fails: nothing would be payable at the enhanced rate to the spouse: the claimant keeps the enhanced rate.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living with a spouse` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 27.05
-- (a) fails: not living with a spouse or partner, so the older child of another person does not matter.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST 27.05
-- (b) fails: the claimant's child is not the only, elder or eldest child paid for, so it is in any other case whatever the household.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living with a spouse` (`a younger child born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2020)) EQUALS JUST 17.90
-- Living with another person as spouse or civil partner (a)(ii), and a polygamous household (a)(iii).
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST 17.90
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST 17.90
-- A polygamous marriage whose members do not reside together is not within (a)(iii): no cut.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST 27.05
-- Several other persons: only the elder or eldest of THEIR children matters to the claimant's child (fork F4). The claimant's child, born 1 January 2011, against an eldest of the others born 1 January 2009.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` (`a claimant with the facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2011)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2009)) EQUALS JUST 17.90

§§ `Regulation 2(2) against paragraphs (4) and (5): FORK F2`

-- (4) removes the claimant's enhanced rate before (2) is reached, so (2)(b) is not met and the claimant's child is in any other case, not for the couple rule.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living with a spouse` (`the only or eldest child, living with a parent of the child, born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2012)) EQUALS JUST 17.90
-- FORK F2. (5) gives the enhanced rate back to the claimant's elder child; (2)(b) reads "would, but for this paragraph, be payable ... at the enhanced rate" and so counts it, and (2) then keeps the enhanced rate for the elder only.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living with a spouse` (`the only or eldest child, living with a parent of the child, born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `a pension increase for the child` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2012)) EQUALS JUST 27.05
-- FORK F2, the claimant's child being the younger of the two: (2) takes it away from the (5)-route child as it would from any other.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living with a spouse` (`the only or eldest child, living with a parent of the child, born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `a pension increase for the child` (`another person whose child counts` TRUE (Date 1 1 2010)) EQUALS JUST 17.90

§§ `Regulation 2(1): a child or qualifying young person (src:18, src:13-15)`

-- Child benefit is not payable for the child: reg 2(1) fixes the rate of child benefit "payable in respect of a child", so with none payable there is no rate to fix: not covered, and never 0.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`a child for whom child benefit is not payable, born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`the enhanced rate would, but for paragraph (2), be payable for the child` `a claimant living alone` (`a child for whom child benefit is not payable, born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment`)

-- Neither a child nor a qualifying young person: reg 2(1) fixes no rate.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`a person with the facts` (Date 1 1 2002) FALSE `in Great Britain` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A qualifying young person in Great Britain (SSCBA test met): the enhanced rate for the only child.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`a person with the facts` (Date 1 1 2008) FALSE `in Great Britain` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 27.05
-- Only the Northern Ireland test is met but the person is in Great Britain: not a qualifying young person.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`a person with the facts` (Date 1 1 2008) FALSE `in Great Britain` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A qualifying young person in Northern Ireland.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`a person with the facts` (Date 1 1 2008) FALSE `in Northern Ireland` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 27.05
-- A child is a child wherever; a qualifying-young-person flag is not needed.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` `a week of 2026` `a claimant living alone` (`a person with the facts` (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE `in neither Great Britain nor Northern Ireland` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 27.05
#ASSERT `the person is a child or a qualifying young person` (`a person with the facts` (Date 1 1 2020) TRUE `in Great Britain` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is a child or a qualifying young person` (`a person with the facts` (Date 1 1 2002) FALSE `in neither Great Britain nor Northern Ireland` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))

§§ `The week: in force from 10 April 2006 (src:9), and the figures of the version of 6 April 2026 (fork F8)`

-- Before the Regulations came into force: not covered.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` (Date 3 4 2006) `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2000)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` (Date 9 4 2006) `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2000)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Between commencement and the version date of the text: the text dates neither figure, so not covered.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` (Date 10 4 2006) `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2000)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` (Date 5 4 2026) `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The version date itself, and after.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` (Date 6 4 2026) `a claimant living alone` (`the only or eldest child born on` (Date 1 1 2010)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 27.05
#ASSERT `the weekly rate for` (Date 13 4 2026) `a claimant living alone` (`a younger child born on` (Date 1 1 2012)) `no payment` `nobody else` EQUALS JUST 17.90
#ASSERT `the figures in regulation 2(1) are those of the text in the week beginning` (Date 6 4 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`the figures in regulation 2(1) are those of the text in the week beginning` (Date 5 4 2026))
